     "body": "<p>I have some local in-progress code that does this as part of <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-api-x/issues/94\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">fcrepo4-labs/fcrepo-api-x#94</a>, which I'd be happy to refactor into a PR to fcrepo-camel, since there seems to be a broader interest in doing so.</p>\n\n<p>On a related note, the existing fcrepo-camel-toolbox SparqlUpdateProcessor currently relies on the fact that all triples share the same subject.  For resources that contain hash URIs, it relies on the fact that a given fedora impl emits messages for the resource <em>and all hash resources</em> defined in it.  The messaging spec doesn't (and probably won't?) specify this behavior with respect to hash URIs, so it's possible that the default SparqlUpdateProcessor behavior may need to be revisited at some point.  A named graph approach where graphs are named by fedora resource URIs would be a bit more straightforward in this regard.</p>",
     "created": "05/Jan/17 2:18 PM",
     "id": "18352",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12332/comment/18352",
